# COMPOSE / ADD / DADD / SEED / NOISE / STRETCH / BLUR / GBLUR / CADD on the manual's Cassegrain, far field at the
# detector (cmdref: Diffraction / Window & Post-Processing).  NONE first, so no graphics device is asked for.
# COMPOSE arms a 64 x 64 grid of 2e-6 pixels at element 5; ADD propagates and accumulates (peak 8.877e6 at
# 129,129); DADD re-displays; SEED/NOISE photon; STRETCH log10; BLUR and GBLUR convolve the composed image;
# CADD runs its dialog (a stub in this version, see the cmdref); PROPAGATE is listed in HELP but not a command.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
none
compose
5
64
2e-6
add
no
dadd
seed
12345
noise
photon
stretch
log10
blur
1
gblur
4e-6,4e-6
no
cadd
5
no
propagate
# EXPECT: Enter element where image is to be composed: \[0\]: 5\s+Enter number of pixels per side: \[256\]: 64\s+Enter size of pixel: \[1\.000000E-03\]: 2e-6
# EXPECT: Peak intensity= 8\.8773143D\+06; Peak occurs at i=\s+129, j=\s+129\s+Sum of intensity= 3\.3131188D\+08\s+Image added\. Plot composed image\? \[YES\]: no
# EXPECT: Enter noise seed \(any integer 1 to 32,700\): \[12345\]: 12345
# EXPECT: Enter noise type \(PHOton, BACkground, REAd, GAUssian\): \[PHOTON\]: photon
# EXPECT: Enter image stretch type \(LINEAR, LOG10, SQRT\): \[LINEAR\]: log10
# EXPECT: Enter blur kernel peak \(1e0\): \[1\.00000\]: 1
# EXPECT: Enter Gaussian blur kernel width in base units \(0,0\): \[0\.00000,0\.00000\]: 4e-6
# EXPECT: Complex amplitude added\. Plot composed image\? \[YES\]: no
# EXPECT: Unknown command = propagate
# EXPECT-NOT: Must COMpose
# EXPECT-NOT: No data to display
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
